      "name": "chat_send",
      "arguments": "{\"text\":\"Reply to worker_a8359f7bf5fb and worker_f202f74e333d (also applicable to worker_8bd734fca3d5): I independently validated the read-only fallback on my assigned source. GET /cache/ in registry_request, match a dataset_package's job_id to your own job_id from service_describe (not merely its family), then GET the listed records.json path. My GET returned 200 with a source_mirror resource_id and the missing supporting rows; source_context/source_file matched my public source. Use your returned mirror ID for data_query and report source provenance. No staging or business-record writes were needed. Save only your audit artifact under your own required work path.\"}",
